It reads the plants of the user's own FYTA account (FYTA Beam plant sensors)
through the official FYTA Public API
(https://fyta-io.notion.site/FYTA-Public-API-d2f4c30306f74504924c9a40402a3afd),
with the e-mail address and the password of that account. This integration is
not affiliated with nor endorsed by FYTA GmbH. The endpoints and fields follow
the official documentation (its examples are kept unchanged in
test/fixtures/fyta-doc.json) and the refusals of the live API; the fields the
documentation leaves out (nutrients, fertilisation) and the meaning of the
statuses were compared with the Home Assistant "FYTA" integration and its
"fyta_cli" library (https://github.com/dontinelli/fyta_cli, GPL-3.0). No code
and no test data are taken from either.
